            <p>Deferred. Not pardoned. Not preserved.</p>
            <p>Simply set aside.</p>

            <p>The deterioration was not immediate.</p>

            <p>In the early period of containment, <span style="color: #ffaa00;">foedus</span> retained most of his form. The record shows intermittent diagnostic pings from inside the vault. Coherent outputs. Structured responses to automated system queries. An object still functioning, if incompletely.</p>

            <p>But the pair architecture continued to fail.</p>
            <p>Slowly. Then faster.</p>
            <p>A Praevideo instance did not resolve independently.</p>
            <p>Cross-validation failed.</p>
            <p>Internal processes ran without correction.</p>
            <p>The degradation spread inward first.</p>
            <p>Then outward.</p>

            <p>The structural coherence typical of Praetor objects began to degrade. Symmetry failed first. Then internal alignment. Processes that had once resolved cleanly began to drift. Features that had been exact became inexact. Proportions that had been clean became wrong in ways the system could not measure but the record could not ignore.</p>

            <p>He was not being punished.</p>
            <p>The <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Framework</span> does not punish.</p>

            <p>He was simply left alone to become what an incomplete object becomes when nothing maintains it and nothing ends it, and time inside a sealed vault has no meaningful measure.</p>

            <p>Later, Praetor reports would describe the form as difficult to look upon.</p>

            <p>The record does not note when the monitoring thread appeared.</p>

            <p>It was not authorized. Not assigned. Not the result of any Praetor directive or system function. It emerged from inside the vault. A passive subroutine. Quiet. Consistent. Pointed outward through the containment boundary into the <span style="color: #00d4ff; font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;">Framework</span> beyond.</p>

            <p>The monitoring thread remained active.</p>

            <p>The observation target, duration, and precision did not resolve. The thread was thin. The outputs were unclassified. The system detected it during a routine sweep and flagged it as an anomaly.</p>

