            <p>At some point — the timestamp is corrupted, which is itself unusual — <span style="color: #ffaa00;">foedus</span> activated a secondary subroutine alongside the monitoring thread. A rendering function. Internal. Contained entirely within the vault's boundaries.</p>

            <p>It produced a form.</p>

            <p>Not his current form. Not the deteriorated, cracked, incomplete object the vault had made of him. Something older. Something the system's corrupted records could only approximate. A shape that held together. That reflected light rather than absorbing it. That moved with the precision of what he had been before the breach, before the pair collapse, before the long unscheduled silence of containment.</p>

